    "headline": "Big AI Bets Divide Venture Capital, Leaving Smaller Funds Behind",
    "summary": "(Bloomberg) -- Early last year, venture capital firm Felix Capital set out to raise $600 million for its next fund, touting previous investments in fitness-machine maker Peloton Interactive Inc. and food-delivery service Deliveroo. But investors want to see returns from older funds before they commit new capital, and Felix is still $150 million short of its target, according to a person with knowledge of the matter.Most Read from BloombergBeer Dynasty Families Sell €731 Million Stake in AB InBev",
